# scripts/engine/archon/patch/paused-run-cancel.patch
# Lets `workflow cancel` take a paused run, and a running run whose owner is proved gone, keeping the worktree.
# Unpatched, cancel refuses a run that isn't running, and a running run with no owner, and points at abandon, which
# removes the worktree with its uncommitted work, so Wheelhouse never calls it. So a run paused at an ask couldn't be
# stopped by a cancel, a cap or All stop (check 74), and a run that lost its process couldn't be released at all
# (check 92). Any other run behaves as released. Applied with `git apply` to Archon v0.13.0 (commit 0d39c1f2); see
# docs/engine/archon-upstream-note.md.
